.TH BRIEF.PY 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
brief.py \- the @brief lane: render enriched findings as the daily or weekly CTI digest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brief.py
.BI \-\-enriched " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-daily | \-\-weekly ]
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-text\-out
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B brief.py
.BI \-\-enriched " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-daily | \-\-weekly ]
.B \-\-subject\-only
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent brief.py
.I options
.br
.B python3 $FLEET_CODE/lanes/brief.py
.I options
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brief.py
turns the JSON written by
.BR enrich.py (1),
or by
.B fleet\-db rollup
for the weekly, into the email the security team reads: an HTML page built
for Outlook (inline CSS, table layout, 640 pixels wide), an optional
plain-text version, and the subject line. It is run by
.BR run\-digest (1),
once to render and once with
.B \-\-subject\-only
to get the subject it passes to
.BR mailer.py (1).
.PP
The digest contains, in order: a header with the organisation name; a lead
sentence counting what the scanner confirmed present (or, failing that,
how many exploited CVEs it could not check); five count tiles, Sev5 to
Sev1; a DEGRADED banner naming any enrichment source that did not answer; a
CISA KEV banner when the input's
.B kev_deadlines
reports a finding past its due date, or one due within 14 days; one section per band; the email subjects the ingest read, up to
60, when the input lists them; and a footer with provenance, the
presence disclaimer and the credit line.
.PP
Each finding shows its CVE linked to NVD, host count, KEV (with due date),
RANSOMWARE, CVSS, EPSS and status badges, a NEW badge or the date first
seen, the rationale, the NVD description (320 characters), the Jira ticket
when one exists, up to 8 QIDs, up to 6 distinct hosts (labelled when they
are
.B host\-xxxxxxxx
pseudonyms), and the scanner's reason. Rows listed per band:
.PP
.EX
Band   daily  weekly
Sev5      99      99
Sev4      12      15
Sev3      12      15
Sev2      10      12
Sev1       0       0
.EE
.PP
Sev1 is counted in the tiles and never listed. A truncated band says how
many more it holds. The plain text applies the same limits.
.PP
The subject is the first of these that applies:
.PP
.EX
[Sev5] CTI Mon DD: N exploited vulns present in the environment
[OVERDUE] CTI Mon DD: N CISA KEV deadlines passed, worst by Dd
CTI Mon DD: N confirmed present, no Sev5
CTI Mon DD: 0 confirmed present, N exploited CVEs the scanner could not check
CTI Mon DD: no new CVEs in the last 24h
CTI Mon DD: N CVEs reviewed, nothing exploitable found
.EE
.PP
The Sev5 form gains
.B "\(em N KEV deadlines OVERDUE"
when any are; the confirmed-present form gains
.B ", N unverified"
when UNKNOWN rows sit in Sev3 or Sev2.
.PP
The weekly says
.B CTI Weekly Mon DD
and
.BR "the last 7 days" .
Dates are local time.
.PP
.B brief.py
only renders. It sends nothing and calls no network service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-enriched " FILE"
Required. The JSON to render. Missing
.B counts
and
.B findings
default to empty,
.B total
to the number of findings, and
.B generated
to now. Ticket keys are read from
.IR FILE \-tickets.json
beside it (the
.I .json
suffix replaced), written by
.BR cti\-jira (1);
a missing or unreadable ticket file is silently ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-daily
Daily row limits, subject and heading. The default.
.TP
.B \-\-weekly
Weekly row limits, subject and heading. Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-daily .
.TP
.B \-\-subject\-only
Print the subject on standard output and exit; nothing is written and
.B \-\-out
is not needed.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Write the HTML digest. Required unless
.BR \-\-subject\-only .
Missing directories are created.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-out " FILE"
Also write the plain-text version: subject, band counts, degraded sources,
new and previously reported counts, KEV deadlines, then each listed finding
with its status, host count, rationale and ticket. Ignored with
.BR \-\-subject\-only .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B brief.py
does not load
.I fleet.env
itself;
.B run\-digest
sources it first. On a hand run through
.BR cti\-agent (1)
these are unset unless exported, and the defaults apply.
.TP
.B FLEET_ORG
Organisation name in the header and default footer.
Default:\~\fBSecurity\fR.
.I fleet.env
section 4.
.TP
.B FLEET_REPO_URL
A link for the credit line. Only
.B http://
and
.B https://
URLs are used; anything else is ignored with a message on standard error.
Setting it alone makes the credit read
.BI "Correlated and published by the " FLEET_ORG " Claude Code Agent Fleet"\fR.
Section 4.
.TP
.B FLEET_ATTRIBUTION
The credit line text. Unset, with no
.BR FLEET_REPO_URL :
.BI "Generated by the " FLEET_ORG " CTI agent fleet"\fR.
Section 4.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/enriched\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.json
The daily's input;
.I weekly\-enriched\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.json
is the weekly's.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/enriched\-YYYY\-MM\-DD\-tickets.json
Ticket map from
.BR cti\-jira ,
optional.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/digest\-{daily,weekly}\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.{html,txt}
What
.B run\-digest
asks it to write.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The subject was printed, or the digest was written.
.TP
.B 1
The input could not be read or is not JSON, or an output could not be
written (Python traceback).
.TP
.B 2
.B \-\-out
missing without
.BR \-\-subject\-only ,
.B \-\-enriched
missing,
or both
.B \-\-daily
and
.BR \-\-weekly .
.SH EXAMPLES
Re-render today's daily to look at it, without sending:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent brief.py \-\-daily \e
  \-\-enriched /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/enriched\-$(date +%F).json \e
  \-\-out /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/preview.html \e
  \-\-text\-out /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/preview.txt
.EE
.PP
The subject this week's rollup would carry:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db rollup \-\-days 7 > /tmp/week.json
python3 /opt/cti\-agent/lanes/brief.py \-\-weekly \-\-subject\-only \e
  \-\-enriched /tmp/week.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR enrich.py (1),
.BR fleet\-db (1),
.BR mailer.py (1),
.BR run\-digest (1),
.BR cti\-jira (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
fleet\-kit/README.md, "What lands in the inbox"; RUNBOOK.md section 12.
